    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-1",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Availability and access"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-1-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Exposure settings choose which management endpoints have HTTP routes."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-1-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Exposure does not grant permission to call an endpoint. Spring Security and network rules control access."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-1-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "An application-defined "
        ],
        [
          "SecurityFilterChain",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " must include the intended Actuator rules. Boot no longer supplies its default Actuator security rules in that case."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-1-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Health details are hidden by default. Exposing them can reveal internal services."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-1-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "management.endpoints.web.exposure.include=*",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " exposes all available endpoints. That is not needed for a health check."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-2",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Health check configuration"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-2-example-0",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Expose the health endpoint",
        "language": "text",
        "description": [
          "Java `17` and Maven are required. The files form a separate project rooted at `pom.xml`.",
          "This application has no Spring Security dependency. It exposes only the health management endpoint.",
          "The request runs in another terminal after startup."
        ],
        "code": "",
        "explanation": [
          "`health` combines the results of configured health checks, such as database connectivity.",
          "A healthy application normally returns `{\"status\":\"UP\"}` with HTTP `200`.",
          "An unhealthy application can return a different status and HTTP status code.",
          "This request checks the configured health indicators. It does not exercise every application feature."
        ],
        "commands": "mvn spring-boot:run\n# Another terminal, after startup\ncurl -i http://localhost:8080/actuator/health",
        "files": [
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/DemoApplication.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\n\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class DemoApplication {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "pom.xml",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n         xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd\">\n    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>\n    <parent>\n        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>\n        <version>3.5.16</version>\n        <relativePath/>\n    </parent>\n    <groupId>com.example</groupId>\n    <artifactId>demo</artifactId>\n    <version>1.0.0</version>\n    <properties><java.version>17</java.version></properties>\n    <dependencies>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n        </dependency>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-actuator</artifactId>\n        </dependency>\n    </dependencies>\n    <build>\n        <finalName>demo</finalName>\n        <plugins>\n            <plugin>\n                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>\n            </plugin>\n        </plugins>\n    </build>\n\n</project>\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/resources/application.properties",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "management.endpoints.web.exposure.include=health\nmanagement.endpoint.health.show-details=never\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-3",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Metrics"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-3-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Actuator uses Micrometer, a library that records measurements such as request counts and JVM memory use."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-3-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The "
        ],
        [
          "metrics",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " endpoint lets a caller inspect these measurements."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-3-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "micrometer-registry-prometheus",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " adds an exporter that writes measurements in Prometheus format."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-3-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The "
        ],
        [
          "prometheus",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " endpoint requires explicit HTTP exposure. A Prometheus server periodically reads it."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-lesson-3-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Grafana can display the measurements stored by Prometheus. Neither tool is required for the basic Actuator health endpoint."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
